id "f52a0604-77f9-51c5-948a-710c52c26fe7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129191 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049997 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129191 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186050264 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129191 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129651 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129191 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186129675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129191 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186268870 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129191 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129191 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186351403 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129191 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186388279 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129191 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186394352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129191 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186394359 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129191 #edb/ref 1039 "Swapping the Order of Integration on a Non-Partitioned Region" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129191 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186129010 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129191 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "cb8c80f2-6dcd-568e-812b-91d39a40119c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129342 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129342 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129342 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129342 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186130074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129342 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129342 #edb/ref 1045 "Changing the Order of Integration in Double Integrals" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129342 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186130071 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129342 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048986 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129342 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "40540042-d3fd-5add-a52b-682e9eaa6e90" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129653 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186127399 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129653 #edb/ref 1069 "q-38468" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129653 #edb/ref 1071 "What is $\\displaystyle \\int_{0}^{4}\\displaystyle \\int_{\\sqrt{x}}^{2}\\cos (y^{3} + π)dydx$?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186129653 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0f89123a-9404-5b9b-b3f7-2ab98adca8fb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130071 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130071 #edb/ref 1061 26536 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130071 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e13e6db5-65c2-53ea-9644-faae6ec26f16" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130071 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186130399 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130072 #edb/ref 1061 26537 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130072 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d45a7233-e073-55c6-8a71-375178f2f11a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130072 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129189 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130073 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130072 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130073 #edb/ref 1061 26538 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130073 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "981fea3c-a71a-5567-bcaf-63176b8545f5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130073 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129190 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130074 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186130073 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130074 #edb/ref 1061 26540 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130074 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "768398f5-6108-549e-9288-fd51dc694028" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130074 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186129191 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130399 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we want to evaluate the repeated integral\n\n$$\n\\int_{\\color{black}0}^{\\color{black}2} \\int_{\\color{black}x/2}^{\\color{black}1} \\, e^{y^2}\\,\\textrm{d}{\\color{black}y} \\, \\textrm{d}{\\color{black}x}.\n$$\n\nThe expression \"$\\,\\textrm{d}y\\,\\textrm{d}x\\,$\" tells us that we should integrate first with respect to $y.$ This is problematic, though, as the integrand $e^{y^2}$ does not have an elementary antiderivative. So, what can we do?\n\nIn cases like this, **reversing the order of integration** from $\\, \\textrm{d}y\\,\\textrm{d}x\\,$ to $\\, \\textrm{d}x\\,\\textrm{d}y$ might help. But beware! Because the domain of integration is non-rectangular, we can't just swap the order of the integrals. This is because, to integrate with respect to $x,$ we can't have $x$'s in the limits. So we need to work out new limits.\n\nWhen swapping the order of integration, it is helpful to sketch the region $D$ over which we're integrating.\n\n![](images/d3/d3ee76083ae3917b4585fce7227475d3e0471550f193f2fa437be3ebf92dc288.png)\n\nTo integrate first with respect to $y,$ we imagine a line parallel to the $y$-axis, as shown above. Note the following:\n\n- This line *enters* the region through the curve $\\color{black} y=\\dfrac{x}{2}$ and *leaves* at $\\color{black} y=1.$ These are the variable limits for $y.$\n\n- The minimum value of $x$ is $\\color{black}0,$ and the maximum value of $x$ is ${\\color{black}2}.$\n\nSo, the integral we were initially given is over the following type I region:\n\n$$\nD=\\left \\{  (x,y) \\: : \\: {\\color{black}0} \\leq x \\leq {\\color{black}2}, \\quad {\\color{black}\\dfrac{x}{2}} \\leq y \\leq {\\color{black}1} \\right\\}\n$$\n\nHowever, since we now want to integrate first with respect to $x,$ we need the limits for $x$ to be functions of $y$, and we need the limits of $y$ to be constants. To work these out, we redraw the region, but this time we imagine a line parallel to the $x$-axis.\n\n![](images/c8/c80ae995a92aba4f535b5e5a01305f8ffbf790ad1f97ee8db4f368e4bfabb0c1.png)\n\n- The line *enters* the region at $\\color{black}x=0$ and *leaves* the region at $\\color{black} x=2y.$ So these are our variable limits for $x.$\n\n- The minimum value of $\\color{black}y$ is $\\color{black}0,$ and the maximum value of $y$ is ${\\color{black}1}.$\n\nSo, we can consider $D$ to be the following type II region:\n\n$$\nD=\\left \\{  (x,y):\\quad {\\color{black}0} \\leq x \\leq {\\color{black}2y}, \\quad {\\color{black}0} \\leq y \\leq {\\color{black}1} \\right\\}\n$$\n\nNow that we have expressed the region $D$ as a type II region, we're ready to swap the order of integration and finally calculate our integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{x/2}^{1}\\,{e}^{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{2y}{e}^{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{2y}\\text{d}x]\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{e}^{{y}^{2}}[x]_{0}^{2y}\\,dy \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2y{e}^{{y}^{2}}dy \\\\  & ={[{e}^{{y}^{2}}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =e-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130399 #edb/ref 1065 4357 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130399 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "ccfd99d2-4e17-53c3-8ac5-2394c59be5c5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186130399 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266788 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{16}-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266788 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186266788 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "481ea564-184e-5eee-bfa2-8fb2bb2ee2d9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267668 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{4}-{e}^{-16}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267668 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267668 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a83b6e24-d2a5-5db0-9ccd-aaee20fdee95" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267818 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{4}+1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267818 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267818 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "baafeef2-8a7d-5eed-b135-3d6a094b65a1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267890 #edb/ref 1080 "1-{e}^{8}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267890 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186267890 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c3d3fbe1-a09a-5e04-97b6-73751f2420d2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268159 #edb/ref 1080 "{e}^{8}-{e}^{-2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268159 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268159 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "e4493e91-98e1-555a-9a0a-ff8a68f4d0a8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268472 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186266788 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268472 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267668 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268472 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267818 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268472 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186267890 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268472 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186268159 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268472 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268472 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268472 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186266788 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268472 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "29fadffe-3310-57b0-80ee-40f2f179eb3e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268897 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186268472 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268897 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132638" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268897 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268897 #edb/ref 1071 "Change the order of integration and evaluate the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{x}^{2}}4x{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268897 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2241615f-0c50-5601-a5f3-153a8d9e79c8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186268897 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/26/262e1b0c4e0ddf338c527b487fcadc85baac12712f91cb4c54b771e49add25b9.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,0\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=0,\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=4-{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{4-y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 4,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{4-y}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/48/48c874b069b55599f76a8fe1aa50c5f4db36ff8943d264a107452668d689174b.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{0}^{4-{x}^{2}}4x{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-y}}4x{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-y}}4x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}{e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\cdot 2{x}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{\\sqrt{4-y}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{4}2(4-y){e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={e}^{8y-{y}^{2}}\\,{|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & ={e}^{8(4)-{4}^{2}}-{e}^{8(0)-{0}^{2}} \\\\  & ={e}^{16}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324044 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{2}-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324044 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324044 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "07e55bd6-6c1e-596d-ac6c-9c05dbbbe44a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324921 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}+1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324921 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186324921 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "7253cc11-8000-559b-8d7c-db1c1254dd64" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325347 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{2}+1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325347 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325347 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a2529f23-3645-5577-bf2f-f291f15c0558" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325925 #edb/ref 1080 "\\sqrt{2}-2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325925 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325925 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "dfd7c19f-6755-5300-ba8e-f738d65b0412" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325930 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186325930 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 175