86350791 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351402 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82196" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351402 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351402 #edb/ref 1071 "Change the order of integration in the double integral ${\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2y-2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351402 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0ea5f28c-cad2-5ccc-8c96-f3d93c56996c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351402 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/06/062d32beb0cab13297c21b2eab703fd5e598191c96daa93a9c27337af95a1930.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,2y-2\\le x\\le 2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=2y-2\\,⟹\\,y=\\frac{x+2}{2},\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\ny=1.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,1\\le y\\le \\frac{x+2}{2}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/54/543ffc57d0d32ae9a4bdefa87bd56deb7380061004b7737cf821117b4fb20e2f.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{2y-2}^{2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{1}^{(x+2)/2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351403 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186350795 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351403 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82210" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351403 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351403 #edb/ref 1071 "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351403 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "22d31834-ac96-55f3-b865-c529af31084e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351403 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/82/8287ba53b227ddc36aff486ea8d42a83203940ee265163320c19ad6cdb39089e.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y}\n$$\n\nand the left boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=0.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type II region. The type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/2c/2c9a41f06d7edfbad9756923d9b70f1d0ffd730350d0b7d2d0e109c1bca9f80d.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{x}^{2}}^{1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{y}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351407 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186351051 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351407 #edb/ref 1069 "q-82255" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351407 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351407 #edb/ref 1071 "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x-1}^{\\sqrt{1-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351407 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "dc249fce-0138-5031-8e39-5c0f2472afa8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186351407 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/0e/0e338b779e846bc3f5ac981c93f9cda65b63d654c1152aa423f855d12d7978d9.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type I region, and its type I representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,x-1\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-x}}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type II regions. \n\n![](images/d2/d2d1df8652af81fbcb789ac05a2d1bf43f9b5b12f394159d0eb17b4ecec90042.png)\n\nNotice that the right boundary of the lower region, written in the form $x=x(y),$  is \n\n$\\,$ $x=y+1.$\n\nAlso, the right boundary of the upper region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$\\,$ $x=1-{y}^{2}.$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 0,\\,0\\le x\\le y+1}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 1-{y}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x-1}^{\\sqrt{1-x}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{y+1}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-{y}^{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388286 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388287 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388286 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132564" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388286 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388286 #edb/ref 1071 "By changing the order of integration in the following double integrals, express the following sum as a single double integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388286 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fac1e7c0-0a06-5b8c-ba15-80235cdce89f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388286 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/9a/9a539f69187276895f8f53e2107c1959fefd0aeb7126dcff049569bfc8bc49d3.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. It consists of two type II regions, given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le y\\le 0,\\,-y-2\\le x\\le 0}\\,\\cup \\,{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,y-2\\le x\\le 0}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\nx=y-2\\,⟹\\,y=x+2,\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region is\n\n$$\nx=-y-2\\,⟹\\,y=-x-2.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we write $D$ as a type I region. The type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 0,\\,-x-2\\le y\\le x+2},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/ba/ba9c9132c8efdb811e63bebc05e1f46bc8cbc54bcb8246072013a75d53bcb4df.png)\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y+{\\int }_{0}^{2}{\\int }_{y-2}^{0}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388287 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388288 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388287 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388289 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388287 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388290 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388287 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388291 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388287 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388287 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388287 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388287 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186388292 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388287 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "53604b27-d02f-579a-aedc-0bb673c96dd1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388288 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388288 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388288 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "f813f916-0601-5644-96e2-e5f9a5ca8427" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388289 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{x+2}^{-x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388289 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388289 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "78361b40-3822-5ff5-a714-d5b563b1e308" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388290 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388290 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388290 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "90893bc6-34ed-5503-86ae-a881d5d3d411" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388291 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{-2}^{2}{\\int }_{x+2}^{-x-2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388291 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388291 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4472336e-1218-5ca6-aa7a-105e2edd3835" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388292 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{-2}^{0}{\\int }_{-x-2}^{x+2}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388292 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388292 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ab9ac760-50be-5d7e-9dce-e8de8e4f3fdb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388300 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186388301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388300 #edb/ref 1069 "q-132573" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388300 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388300 #edb/ref 1071 "Change the order of integration in the double integral \n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-1}^{1-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388300 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "446a02c7-d043-54a5-9d35-72c77f70ee6d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388300 #edb/ref 1074 "![](images/e6/e6b8889f9e8025cfca1ee0ae61b67a2f7ec9ec4aee15fab78d2f418a655bbcb8.png)\n\nThe diagram above shows the region of integration. This is a type II region, and its type II representation is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,{y}^{2}-1\\le x\\le 1-y}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration, we need to split $D$ into two type I regions.\n\n![](images/52/52640b30ded8bf2cd19fe7860c7640bde3c8427ae8978f32fb8020b2f7215468.png)\n\nNotice that the bottom and top boundaries of the left region, written in the form $y=y(x),$  are \n\n$\\,$ $y=0\\,$ and $\\,y=\\sqrt{x+1}.$\n\nAlso, the bottom and top boundaries of the right region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $y=0\\,$ and $\\,y=1-x.$ \n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x+1}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le 1-x}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{{y}^{2}-1}^{1-y}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x+1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388303 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388305 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388301 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186388306 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388301 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388301 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388301 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186388304 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388301 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "5a76d6c6-f79c-5e15-b460-5a7e313685d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388302 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x-1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388302 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388302 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d02f7bb8-5ef2-5339-92ed-4d00eb590abf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186388303 #edb/ref 1080 "{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{0}^{\\sqrt{x-1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{1-x}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1